your choice until end of turn.', "Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, that creature's controller mills two cards.", 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, each other player sacrifices a creature.', 'Whenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Forgotten Ancient.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move any number of +1/+1 counters from Forgotten Ancient onto other creatures.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player mills two cards.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature and a +1/+1 counter on Juniper Order Ranger.', "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may put X +1/+1 counters on Hamletback Goliath, where X is that creature's power.", 'Whenever one or more creatures attack, you may have target attacking creature gain double strike until end of turn.', 'Whipflare deals 2 damage to each nonartifact creature.', 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', '[+2]: Discard up to two cards, then draw that many cards.\\n[−2]: Sacrifice an artifact. If you do, return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n[−10]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an artifact is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield at the beginning of the next end step."\\nDaretti, Scrap Savant can be your commander.', '{1}, {T}, Discard a card: You gain 4 life.\\n{1}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Create a 0/1 white Goat creature token.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Draw a card.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', "{1}{B}: Exile target card from an opponent's graveyard. If no cards are in that graveyard, flip Nezumi Graverobber.", '{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Magus of the Wheel: Each player discards their hand, then draws seven cards.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', "{2}{R}, {T}: Create a token that's a copy of target creature card in your graveyard, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types. It gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.", '{3}, {T}: Draw three cards. This ability costs {1} more to activate for each card in your hand.', '{4}, {T}: Put a fate counter on target permanent.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Oblivion Stone: Destroy each nonland permanent without a fate counter on it, then remove all fate counters from all permanents.', "{6}{R}{R}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Stoneshock Giant becomes monstrous, creatures without flying your opponents control can't block this turn.", '{G}: Exile target card from a graveyard. If it was a creature card, put a +1/+1 counter on Scavenging Ooze and you gain 1 life.', '{G}{U}, {T}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target artifact, creature, or land.', '{R}: Inferno Titan gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nWhenever Inferno Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, it deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}, Sacrifice Panic Spellbomb: Target creature can't block this turn.\\nWhen Panic Spellbomb is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may pay {R}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}. You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: You gain 1 life.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity. If you spend this mana to cast your commander, it enters the battlefield with a number of additional +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Dreadship Reef.\\n{1}, Remove X storage counters from Dreadship Reef: Add X mana in any combination of {U} and/or {B}.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Until end of turn, creatures your opponents control lose hexproof and shroud and can't have hexproof or shroud.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Buried Ruin: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{B}{G}: Until end of turn, Svogthos, the Restless Tomb becomes a black and green Plant Zombie creature with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard." It\'s still a land.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ghost Quarter: Destroy target land. Its controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Dreamstone Hedron: Draw three cards.', '{T}: Add {R} or {W}.\\n{R}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Boros Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {R}.', "{T}: Choose any number of target creatures. Each of those creatures gains persist until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", "{T}: Choose target artifact a player controls and target artifact card in that player's graveyard. If both targets are still legal as this ability resolves, that player simultaneously sacrifices the artifact and returns the artifact card to the battlefield.", '{T}: Hammerfist Giant deals 4 damage to each creature without flying and each player.', '{T}: Target permanent becomes an artifact in addition to its other types until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"\'I have arrived,\' bellowed Brawn, and the plane shuddered."\\n—*Scroll of Beginnings*', '"A crafter must imbue her weapon with part of her soul—something the Phyrexians are incapable of doing."\\n—Melira', '"Ach! Hans, run! It\'s the lhurgoyf!"\\n—Saffi Eriksdotter, last words', '"Avacyn has abandoned us! We have nothing left except what we can take!"', '"Behold astronomy\'s contribution to war."\\n—Fennor Rhyl, starcaller', '"Death is no excuse for disobedience."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Even your blade knows who will triumph here."\\n—Atraxa, Praetors\' Voice', '"Fate is not as fixed as you might think."', '"For dim-witted, thick-skulled genetic mutants, they have pretty good aim."\\n—Sisay, captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"Have you ever held a Boros signet? There\'s a weight to it that belies its size—a weight of strength and of pride."\\n—Agrus Kos', '"Her voice is insight, piercing and true."\\n—Ixidor, reality sculptor', '"Holy places are no longer sanctuary from death, and death is no longer sanctuary from anything."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"I have attuned the staff to your screams so that only I may benefit from your pain."\\n—Volux, disciple of Nin', '"I used to hurl rocks and eat scraps of meat burned over a fire. Look at what I\'ve become and tell me Simic does not hold infinite possibility."', '"I wrecked your metal guy, boss. But look! I made you an ashtray."', '"If fear is the only tool you have left, then you\'ll never control me."\\n—Xantcha, to Gix', '"If you live on a giant\'s back, there\'s only one individual you\'ll ever need to fear."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"In case of fire, treachery, citywide riot, political upheaval, or worldwide societal collapse, break glass."\\n—Cluestone inscription', '"It has been my experience that disasters like to strike in pairs."', '"It reflects the purity of Mirrodin-that-was."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s a fine way to travel, if you don\'t mind the smell."', '"Listen to the roar! Feel the thunder! The Immersturm shouts its approval with every bolt of lightning!"', '"Naga shed their scales. We wear ours with pride."\\n—Golran, dragonscale captain', '"Nature is a wonderful engineer but works far too slowly for my tastes."', '"Now the scaled ones rule Tarkir."', '"Obey!"', '"Oh sure, they buy a lot of ale, but I always find myself needing to rebuild after the giants have paid a visit."\\n—Belko, owner of Titan\'s Keg tavern', '"Our glorious infection has taken hold."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Savagery is the birthright of every creature that draws breath—or wishes it could."\\n—Karador, Ghost Chieftain', '"She will come back to me."', '"So even the heart of our world has succumbed."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"Soaring is wasted on the winged."\\n—Edric, Spymaster of Trest', '"Stop thinking like an artificer, Urza, and start thinking like a father!"\\n—Rayne, chancellor of the Tolarian Academy', '"The Filigree Texts do not compel you to act in accordance with their precepts. They only specify the consequences should you fail."\\n—Lodus of the Ethersworn', '"The awestruck birds gazed at Wonder. Slowly, timidly, they rose into the air."\\n—*Scroll of Beginnings*', '"The bonds of loyalty can tie one to the grave."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"The shadow travels toward the apex. I predict we will soon see the true measure of darkness."', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"They\'ll soon become accustomed to wearing skin that is not their own."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Those who are different are untrustworthy, unpredictable. Put your safety in the hands of your own kind."\\n—Bowen, Barrenton guardcaptain', '"Through me, the Great Teacher\'s voice will rattle this world."', '"To fill your mind with knowledge, we must start by emptying it."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Tools and artisans can be destroyed, but the act of creation is inviolate."\\n—Elspeth Tirel', '"Try to pretend like you understand what\'s important."', '"We are all decaying, always in a state of near-death. One moment without breath and we begin to break down."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We must rely on our own knowledge, not on the dogma of the seekers or the mutterings of the sphinxes."\\n—Tullus of Palandius', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"What we knew as Emeria, Ula, and Cosi were not divine beings at all, but a cruel trick, and a grave error."\\n—*The Invokers\' Tales*', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"When something dies, all things benefit. Well okay, just our things."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"Where a lesser mind sees junk, I see infinite potential."', '"Where will you run when I punish you with the very ground you flee on?"\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"You are beneath contempt. Your lineage will be forgotten."', '"You may enter, but leave those lifeless things of your world behind."\\n—Modruni, maro-sorcerer', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', 'A hundred generations has he mentored, a hundred armies has he crushed beneath his feet, yet only a hundred words has he ever spoken, each more revered than a hundred books.', "A single festercreep isn't alone. It's already an infestation.", 'After lightning struck the cliffs, the ore became iron, the iron became steel, and the steel became greaves. The lightning never left.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'An emblem of a secret guild, the Dimir insignia is seen only by its own members—and the doomed.', 'As Glissa searches for the truth about Memnarch, Bosh searches to unearth the secrets of his past.', "Ask your query and be on your way. Just don't look her in the eye.", "Avacyn's holy warriors kept hope alive in her darkest hours. Now they will carry that hope across Innistrad.", 'Boggarts constantly strive to outdo each other with the things they bring back to the warren, each hoping the exploit will become as well-known as those of Auntie Grub.', 'Countless delights drift on the surface while dark schemes run below.', 'Depending on your point of view, the seal represents a proud guardian of the natural cycle or one who has sold her soul to darkness for eternal life.', 'Deserted, but not uninhabited.', 'Disaster stalks with gaping jaws across unready lands.', 'Elementals are ideas given form. This one is the idea of "smashitude."', 'Enduring the most desolate and dangerous conditions, Abzan sentries unfailingly guard the stronghold gates.', 'Even a fragment of a powerstone contains within it not just energy, but space—vast dimensions trapped in fragile crystal.', 'Even baloths fear its feeding time.', "Ever since the disaster, the city's survivors viewed the star-strewn sky with dread.", 'Exhale, and let the winds carry your soul for all eternity.', 'Fools surrender their sanity to his riddles. Even greater fools try to solve them.', 'For the Phyrexians, death is not an end, nor a one-time occurrence.', 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", 'Garbage in, treasure out.', 'Giants share nothing but their fury.', 'Grixis is a world where the only things found in abundance are death and decay. Corpses, whole or in part, are the standard currency among necromancers and demons.', 'He cares not for the disasters his storm brings as long as his path ahead is clear.', 'He collects the precious metals, and then converts the rest to propellant.', 'His verdict is always guilty. His sentence is always death.', 'History has buried its treasures deep.', 'In nature, not a single bone or scrap of flesh goes to waste.', 'Infinite possibilities contained in a finite space.', 'Instead of creating a tool that would be damaged by heat, the Thran built one that was charged by it.', 'It harmonizes with the essence of its master.', 'It is the forest beyond the horizon, the mountain waiting to be climbed, the new land across the endless sea.', 'It is unwise to insult the god of the forge. It is also unwise to stand near anyone else who has insulted him.', 'It promises protection to those in need and proclaims a warning to any who would threaten Ravnican law.', "It's no coincidence that the oldest trolls are also the angriest.", 'Its blood is life. Its body is growth.', 'Its collapse is like the lashing out of a long-dead civilization that resents being forgotten.', 'Its graceful glide paints the ocean floor with strokes of luminescence.', 'Its open mouth is a furnace blast that blisters the skin. Its smoking fists are meteors that split the earth.', 'Its wings beat to the howls of war and fan the fires of rage.', 'Its wings shimmer with dreams absorbed from its enemies.', 'Kuldotha, wellspring of molten metal, temple of the goblin horde.', 'Life is such a fragile thing.', "Light's champion in the stronghold of darkness.", 'Little agonies pave the way to greater power.', 'Loose earth is not a burial but an appetizer.', "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", 'Mages come from far and wide to bathe in its wisdom.', "Many who cross Sorin's path come down with a sudden and fatal case of being-in-the-way-of-a-millennia-old-vampire.", 'Mephidross gives up treasure easily . . . as long as you take its place.', 'Most books simply deliver knowledge. This one expects some in return.', 'Murky Otarian tides hide the forgotten treacheries of the Phyrexian war.', 'Necromancers deal in commodities far more precious than gold and grain.', 'Nothing breaks the monotony like a good old-fashioned riot.', 'Nothing escapes its gaze—or its breath.', 'On Otaria, peace and harmony are rare. Places that provide both are cherished.', 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', 'One quiet word sets off the stampede.', 'Only a thin layer of dirt separates civilization from an undead apocalypse.', 'Only the Eldrazi mind thinks in the warped paths required to open the hedrons and tap the power within.', "Only the sun that beats down upon Arashin's walls could shine more brightly.", 'Reinforcements . . . or refreshments?', 'Remade by Eldrazi magic, Tuktuk inspired an entire clan of misguided goblins.', "She remembers every word spoken, from the hero's oath to the baby's cry.", 'Some see the world as a place of infinite wonder and knowledge. Some see it as an infinite dinner plate.', 'Spitting is the customary greeting between a creature and its magical impostor.', 'Structures built from darksteel yield to neither assault nor age.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'That which endures, survives.', 'The Abzan turn to this spell only as a last resort, for its inevitable result is what they most dread: to be alone.', 'The Orzhov care not for repentance, only repayment.', 'The Phyrexian death machine awoke, its coldsteel heart imbuing it with sinister new power.', "The arbiter Galanda Feudkiller judges Lorwyn's squabbles from a lofty perspective.", 'The best techniques outlive their creators.', 'The corruption stirred the heavens above, awaking a shining champion.', 'The dense jungle surrenders to a lush and lavish expanse. At its center uncoil the spires of Qarsi Palace.', 'The fastest way across the dunes is above.', "The form of the sigil is just as important as the sigil itself. If it's carried on a medallion, its bearer is a master. If it's tattooed on the body, its bearer is a slave.", 'The knights see a mighty quarry. The dragon sees breakfast, lunch, and dinner.', 'The kor send their thopter kites to see if the land is in a welcoming mood.', 'The light sigh of its breath whistles through its bones.', 'The myr are like the Glimmervoid: blank canvases on which to build grand creations.', 'The oil created the mycosynth. The mycosynth created New Phyrexia.', 'The power of a waterfall. The fury of an avalanche. The intellect of a gale-force wind.', 'The scrape of shovels and the tumble of cold dirt soon muffled their pleas.', 'The slag-workers wasted no time in creating their own flare pulses to cleanse the area of the *incompleat*.', 'There are many ruins, but there used to be many more.', 'They fell screaming into the depths of the chasm like so many pebbles tossed down a well.', 'Those who bring nothing to the temple take nothing away.', "Though giants are mortal, they live so long and on such a grand scale that many small folk don't believe they ever truly die.", 'To protect the alliance between Kjeldor and Yavimaya, they trained in the ways of both.', 'Weakness is not in the nature of the Swarm.', 'When defeat is near and guidance is scarce, all eyes look in one direction.', "When tempers run high, it's easy to lose your head.", 'When the moon rises and the bloodlust takes hold, nothing matters but the kill.', 'Whether trained, ridden, or eaten, few goblin military innovations have rivaled the bug.', 'Without the interfering hands of civilization, nature will always shape itself to its own needs.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Alisa Lee', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Austin Hsu', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brandon Dorman', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Carl Frank', 'Charles Gillespie', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Ciruelo', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Rapoza', 'Dermot Power', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Donato Giancola', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Fortune', 'Eric Peterson', 'Eric Velhagen', 'Erica Yang', 'Eytan Zana', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Harper', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Hildebrandt & Tim Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Henry G. Higginbotham', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Ironbrush', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Zapata', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Larry MacDougall', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lindsey Look', 'Mark A. Nelson', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael Bruinsma', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Sass', 'Min Yum', 'Monte Michael Moore', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Nottsuo', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Paolo Parente & Brian Snõddy', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Puddnhead', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Reb